# Line endings.
#
# The repo is authored on Windows and deployed on Linux. Git's autocrlf warned
# about every file during the first `git add` — harmless for most of them, but
# NOT for the shell scripts: a deploy script checked out with CRLF fails on the
# server with "$'\r': command not found", and the error points at the line after
# the real one. It is a genuinely horrible half-hour to debug.
#
# So the two deploy scripts are pinned to LF everywhere, working copy included.

* text=auto

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.prisma text eol=lf

# These only ever run on Windows and want CRLF.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
